<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕverso</span></b> , āre,
			v. freq. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to turn round</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versa et reversa in tergum et in latera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Conf. 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">panis qui non reversatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Os. 7, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subcinericius panis est cinere coctus et
					reversatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. 20, 2, 15</span></i>
			.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mid.: reversatur ejus ex talis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 3, 11</span></i>
			.— <i>Pass.</i> reversatus, <i>turned back</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palpebra ejus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. Val. 1, 23</span></i>
			.</div>
